<title>BRAZIL: Brazil soybean plantings 83 pct completed - Safras.</title>
<headline>Brazil soybean plantings 83 pct completed - Safras.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian soybean plantings were 83 percent completed by December 5 against 78 percent by the same period last year and an average of the past five years of 84 percent, consultants Safras e Mercado said.</p>
<p>Plantings by November 28 this year were 72 percent.</p>
<p>Irregular weather however made work in the field difficult. In the southern region, rains slowed down plantings. Most progress was seen in the center-west with the exception of Goias which saw excess rainfall.</p>
<p>-- Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151</p>
</text>
